From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Fri, 17 Oct 2026 04:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] sg2000 module: bring the WiFi/BT board init in line
 with the Milk-V Duo S

Milk-V states the Duo Module 01 EVB runs DuoS software directly, and the
working DuoS u-boot board init (duo-buildroot-sdk-v2,
sg2000_milkv_duos_glibc_arm64_sd) carries three things our grafted board
dir lacked:

  - PINMUX_CONFIG(CLK32K, PWR_GPIO_10): the 32.768 kHz LPO clock to the
    module. Without it the AIC8800 power-on handshake over SDIO times
    out after ~2 s ("fail to set AIC_WIFI power state to 1") and the
    radio never enumerates;
  - set_rtc_register_for_power(): mmio 0x050260D0 = 0x7, RTC-domain
    power for the module WiFi/BT block;
  - UART2 -> UART4 remux for the module BT HCI UART.

The Wi-Fi power pins (porta15/porte7) already matched the Duo S.
Also un-breaks the SLIP UART1 mmio writes: the previous append left
them dead-coded behind an early 'return 0'.

---
diff --git a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duomodule01_sd/u-boot/cvi_board_init.c b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duomodule01_sd/u-boot/cvi_board_init.c
index 93c39f4..fa4719e 100644
--- a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duomodule01_sd/u-boot/cvi_board_init.c
+++ b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duomodule01_sd/u-boot/cvi_board_init.c
@@ -1,19 +1,36 @@
-// Milk-V Duo Module 01 Evaluation Board — u-boot pinmux.
 //
 // Minimal headless RNSBox config: UART0 and SD run on their reset
 // multiplexing, so the only pins that need explicit setup are the
-// internal GbE PHY LEDs (same wiring as the Milk-V Duo S reference).
+// internal GbE PHY LEDs (same wiring as the Milk-V Duo S reference)
+// plus the module WiFi/BT bring-up (identical to the Milk-V Duo S:
+// 32k LPO clock to the module, RTC-domain power, BT HCI on UART4).
+static void set_rtc_register_for_power(void)
+{
+	// Milk-V Duo S: RTC-domain power for the module WiFi/BT block.
+	mmio_write_32(0x050260D0, 0x7);
+}
+
 int cvi_board_init(void)
 {
 	// Internal GbE PHY LEDs
 	PINMUX_CONFIG(PWR_WAKEUP0, EPHY_LNK_LED);
 	PINMUX_CONFIG(PWR_BUTTON1, EPHY_SPD_LED);
 
-	return 0;
+	// Module WiFi/BT (same as the Milk-V Duo S): 32k LPO clock to the
+	// module, RTC power register. Without the LPO clock the AIC8800
+	// power-on handshake times out ("fail to set AIC_WIFI power state").
+	PINMUX_CONFIG(CLK32K, PWR_GPIO_10);
+	PINMUX_CONFIG(UART2_RX, UART4_RX);
+	PINMUX_CONFIG(UART2_TX, UART4_TX);
+	PINMUX_CONFIG(UART2_CTS, UART4_CTS);
+	PINMUX_CONFIG(UART2_RTS, UART4_RTS);
+	set_rtc_register_for_power();
 
 	// UART1 (SLIP to the HaLow modem): XGPIOA[28] TX / XGPIOA[29] RX,
 	// fmux func=1 — the same encoding the Sipeed SG2002 boards use for
 	// these pads.
 	mmio_write_32(0x03001070, 0x1); // GPIOA 28 UART1 TX
 	mmio_write_32(0x03001074, 0x1); // GPIOA 29 UART1 RX
+
+	return 0;
 }
